From: Chromium Authors
Subject: [cff] Validate operand type for charset and Encoding operators

Enforce DICT_OPERAND_INTEGER for charset (case 15) and Encoding (case 16)
operands in the CFF1 parser before checking predefined constants (first <= 2
and first <= 1).

Without this check, Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) operands, which OTS stores with
a dummy integer value of 0 and DICT_OPERAND_REAL type, satisfy the predefined
range check and skip CheckOffset, allowing unvalidated offsets to pass through.

This is a subset of upstream commit
5c681204ed7ec95971598b27d247247b3aa4d78b (PR #314), which introduces the
Operand class; this change should be subsumed under a future OTS roll.

Bug: 505807063
---
 src/cff.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cff.cc b/src/cff.cc
index af54a4a..bc64136 100644
--- a/src/cff.cc
+++ b/src/cff.cc
@@ -778,6 +778,9 @@ bool ParseDictData(ots::Buffer& table, ots::Buffer& dict,
         if (operands.size() != 1) {
           return OTS_FAILURE();
         }
+        if (operands.back().second != DICT_OPERAND_INTEGER) {
+          return OTS_FAILURE();
+        }
         if (operands.back().first <= 2) {
           // predefined charset, ISOAdobe, Expert or ExpertSubset, is used.
           break;
@@ -795,6 +798,9 @@ bool ParseDictData(ots::Buffer& table, ots::Buffer& dict,
         if (operands.size() != 1) {
           return OTS_FAILURE();
         }
+        if (operands.back().second != DICT_OPERAND_INTEGER) {
+          return OTS_FAILURE();
+        }
         if (operands.back().first <= 1) {
           break;  // predefined encoding, "Standard" or "Expert", is used.
         }
